From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:10:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] brick_defconfig cut down to the Brick: no USB host (the
 gadget stays), cameras, video or 2D engines, loop or RAM disks, netfilter,
 PPP, bridging, VLANs or IPv6, PC-era input or SysRq; and none of the
 debugging that slowed every allocation, lock and preemption (SLUB_DEBUG_ON,
 DEBUG_VM, DEBUG_MUTEXES, DEBUG_PREEMPT), nor PM debug, virtual terminals,
 cgroups, swap or CFQ. The LRADC keyboard stays though it never reports, as
 TortOS opens its input devices by number. 12.7 MB to 10.2 MB; the kernel
 reaches its first program in about 0.6 s instead of 1.8. The lists are in
 brick-spike/trim

---
 arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig | 158 ++++-------------------------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 139 deletions(-)

